architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:199:- `ThreeView.vue` contains no `new THREE.`, `scene.children`, `Float32BufferAttribute`, `LineBasicMaterial`, `MeshBasicMaterial`, `SphereGeometry`, `TubeGeometry`, `PlaneGeometry`, `ArrowHelper`, `CSS2DObject`, `world.projectionPlanes`, `getAll3DPoints`, `getAll3DLines`, `getAll3DSegments`, `getAllPlanes`, `getAllHingeLines`, `getLine2D`, `isGuideLine`, `isPerpendicularGuide`, `calculateGuidePlaneNormal`, `realize2D(world)`, or `realize3D(world)`. The only allowed flow is UI display/selected IDs + injected `World` into runtime/controller refresh.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:201:- `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/**` contains no imports from Vue, Pinia, `OrbitControls`, `CSS2DRenderer`, `CSS2DObject`, `WebGLRenderer`, or `Scene` adapter classes. Selector files remain concern-split (`ProjectionPlane3DSelector`, `PlanarElement3DSelector`, `ReconstructedElement3DSelector`, `Guide3DSelector`, `Hinge3DSelector`/axis equivalent) rather than one god selector.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:228:- ThreeView shell: passes display options, injected `World`, and selected IDs to the runtime/controller, and contains no geometry, selected-domain-lookup, scene setup, label construction, or `scene.children` clearing logic.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:234:- Lifecycle: mount, scene setup extraction, refresh on world/display/selection changes, resize, grouped object replacement, CSS2D label cleanup/replacement, and full disposal.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:255:`ThreeView.vue` is only a lifecycle/composition shell. It may read `viewStore`, `selectionStore`, and the injected `World` to assemble shell inputs, but it must pass selected IDs and display state into the application boundary as an explicit `threePresentation` input, for example `ThreePresentationInput { world, displayOptions, selectedIds }`. The component must not perform direct selected-element domain lookup, guide/perpendicular-plane derivation, projection-plane matrix interpretation, domain-to-view coordinate conversion, or raw Three.js object construction.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:257:Selected guide behavior belongs outside the component. `Guide3DSelector` consumes selected IDs, resolves guide eligibility/realizations through domain APIs, and emits guide perpendicular-plane and guide intersection marker DTOs. `GuideSceneAdapter` consumes those DTOs and creates/replaces scene objects. `ThreeView.vue` only calls `runtime.refresh(input)` and never constructs guide/perpendicular-plane DTOs or Three.js guide objects.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:263:- `ProjectionPlane3DSelector`: projection-plane surfaces, grids, mesh extents, reference axes, auxiliary axes, and projection-plane/axis labels.
architecture-audit/cycle-008-3d-rendering-scene-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:264:- `PlanarElement3DSelector`: 2D-on-3D-plane point/line/segment/circle DTOs and explicit line extent/style/z-offset metadata.
